WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:07.630
Your AI agent writes code all day — but ask it to tidy your windows, and it's stuck.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:13.093
So let's give it eyes. And hands.

00:00:13.843 --> 00:00:20.193
I'll just say it the way I'd tell a friend: TextEdit top right, Calculator bottom right.
you: put TextEdit in the top-right quarter and Calculator in the bottom-right quarter of my main monitor

00:00:26.293 --> 00:00:32.848
It picks up the windowctl skill on its own... and there it is. Done.
you: put TextEdit in the top-right quarter and Calculator in the bottom-right quarter of my main monitor

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:41.958
Now, point at the seven, with a green arrow... and there it is, right on the button.
you: point at the 7 button on Calculator with a green arrow saying press 7, and keep it on screen

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:48.461
Here's the one that gets me. Find the Format menu, and circle it.
you: find the Format menu in TextEdit and circle it, keep it on screen

00:00:51.658 --> 00:00:57.988
It doesn't guess at pixels — it asks the app where that menu actually lives.
you: find the Format menu in TextEdit and circle it, keep it on screen

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:03.721
And when we're finished? Clean up the arrows. Gone.
you: clean up the arrows

00:01:11.508 --> 00:01:19.401
And it works from a script, or CI, too. One line — no chat window at all.
$ claude -p "put TextEdit on the left half and point at its Format menu" --dangerously-skip-permissions

00:01:21.458 --> 00:01:25.335
...and the desktop just follows along.
$ claude -p "put TextEdit on the left half and point at its Format menu" --dangerously-skip-permissions

00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:35.162
One binary. Every screen. Go make your desktop work for you.
npm install -g @muthuishere/windowctl
